OL,3,AHow could Israel break election
OL,4,Adeadlock? Here are four scenarios
OL,5,
OL,6,FIsrael looks to be in political
OL,7,Fdeadlock.
OL,9,FWith 85% of votes counted after
OL,10,FTuesday's election, neither the
OL,11,Fincumbent Prime Minister Benjamin
OL,12,FNetanyahu's coalition, nor the bloc of
OL,13,Fhis key challenger Gadi Eisenkot look
OL,14,Fset to win a majority.
OL,16,FIn order to form a government, it looks
OL,17,Flikely one of the leading parties would
OL,18,Fhave to break their campaign promises -
OL,19,Fmeaning the most probable outcome may
OL,20,Fwell be new elections.
OL,22,FHere are four possible scenarios.
OL,23,APub: 28-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
